course: dictionary
lesson: 2769
title: Discover: find, learn, or notice
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: «Uranus was the first planet discovered with a telescope, found by William Herschel in Bath, England, in 1781.» Discover means to find something for the first time, or to find something that was hidden or unknown. Here, nobody had seen Uranus before, and then someone found it.
explain: Discover also means to find out a fact, or learn something you did not know before. «Archimedes discovered how things float» means he learned a rule that nobody had known before. Discovering can also mean noticing or starting to enjoy something new: «She discovered a love of painting.»
explain: Use the words around discover to check its meaning. Planet, telescope and scientists tell you it is about finding new things. Then swap in found: «Galileo found Jupiter's four biggest moons» still makes sense, so found is a good check here.
fact: Discover is a verb: discover, discovers, discovered, discovering.
fact: «Discover» means to find something for the first time, or to find out something you did not know before.
fact: «Galileo discovered Jupiter's four biggest moons, Io, Europa, Ganymede and Callisto, in 1610 with one of the first telescopes.»
fact: Often local people already knew an animal; when scientists «discovered» it, they described and named it.
fact: You can also make a discovery, such as a new planet, a new medicine or a new pattern in maths.
exercise: «Uranus was the first planet discovered with a telescope.» What does discovered mean here? | Lost in space | *Found for the first time | Painted a bright colour | Sold to a museum
exercise: «Archimedes discovered how things float.» What did Archimedes do? | *Learned a fact he did not know before | Built a boat for the king | Bought a new bath | Forgot how to swim
exercise: Mia says, «I discovered a love of painting last summer.» What does she mean? | She was given a painting for her birthday | She found a lost paintbrush | *She noticed and started to enjoy painting | She sold all her paintings
test: In maths, Sam discovers a pattern in the numbers. What does discovers mean? | Forgets the numbers | Gives the numbers to his teacher | *Finds out a rule he did not know before | Writes the numbers in a neat list
test: Why do we say scientists discovered an animal that local people already knew? | *Because scientists described and named it | Because local people had hidden it from the world | Because the animal was made in a laboratory | Because it was a planet
exam: «Galileo discovered Jupiter's moons in 1610.» Which word means about the same as discovered here? | Lost | Sold | Painted | *Found
